Remove a hub, hopspace, or branch.

Removing a branch worktree runs a safety gate first. A branch merged into
the default branch (merge commit, squash, or rebase) with a clean worktree
is removed silently. Anything else needs explicit flags:

  merged, uncommitted or untracked files         --no-verify
  not merged, pushed to origin, clean            --force
  not merged, pushed, uncommitted or untracked   --force --no-verify
  not merged, not pushed                         --force --no-verify

--force covers the not-merged check; --no-verify covers uncommitted or
untracked files (merged or not) and unpushed commits. Neither implies
the other: pushing protects commits, not the files in the worktree.
--no-prompt only skips the confirmation prompt; it never satisfies the
gate. --no-verify does not skip pre-/post-worktree-remove hooks.

Usage:
  git-hop remove [target] [flags]

Aliases:
  remove, rm, delete, del

Flags:
      --delete-remote   Also delete the branch on origin; without it removal stays local and never contacts the network
  -h, --help            help for remove
      --merged          Remove all worktrees whose branch is merged into the default branch (skips the default branch itself and the active worktree)
      --no-prompt       Skip the confirmation prompt only; does NOT bypass the safety gate
      --no-verify       Allow removal despite uncommitted/untracked files or unpushed commits; does NOT bypass the not-merged check (needs --force)

Global Flags:
  -n, --dry-run         preview changes without applying
      --force           bypass safety checks
      --format string   Output format (csv, human, json, table, text, yaml) (default "table")
  -g, --global          use global hopspace in $GIT_HOP_DATA_HOME (default: local)
      --json            output in JSON format
      --no-color        Disable ANSI color
      --no-hints        Suppress next-step hints after command output
      --offline         Disable network access. Highest-precedence override: flips off per-command network opt-ins (peer discovery, sync, GitHub, push). Enforced beneath net/http and any client routed through netpolicy.GuardDial; loopback and diagnostics stay exempt.
      --porcelain       machine-readable output
  -q, --quiet           Suppress non-essential output
  -V, --verbose count   Increase log verbosity (-V=debug, -VV=trace)
